/*
 * Spawn Configuration system copyright (©) 2025 TacticalToaster
 * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
 * I recommend don't change any config if you don't know what it does.
 * Config Notation: Patrol, Checkpoint and Hunt squads all use the same explicit formation format.
 * "patrolChance", "checkpointChance" or "huntChance": 100 = 100% chance to spawn the configured squad, 50 = 50%, etc.
 * "squadCount" or "holdZonesCount": Number of squads/locations selected by that spawn system.
 * "primaryWildtype": WildType used as BossName / primary bot for the BossLocationSpawn entry.
 * "formation": Literal WildType -> exact bot count. Any registered custom WildType can be added without changing the spawn code.
 * Example: { "ISBTeamLeader": 1, "ISBSecondLeader": 2, "ISBSpecialForces": 3 } = exactly 6 bots.
 * Existing variable min/max sizes were migrated to one fixed formation using the rounded midpoint of the old range.
 *
 * Hunts are a special type of patrol that actively hunt targets on the map in the following order of priority:
 * Black Div --> PMC Bots --> Hostile Bots --> Player.
 * They spawn instantly when active, and the spawn chance is determined by a random draw.
 * Empty hunt zones cause the hunt squads to spawn in any zone
 *
 * Patrols are ISB groups that simply patrol the map and eliminate targets within range.
 * In this configuration, they will ALWAYS spawn at the end of raids when their spawn chance is drawn
 *
 * Checkpoints are ISB groups that spawn at fixed points on the map and eliminate targets within range.
 * After spawning, they remain stationary at that point, protecting it.
 * They spawn instantly when active, and the spawn chance is determined by a random draw.
 */
